filter_frames.py and sample.py are only relevant when we don't want to use the manually selected frames.

Instead, we sample a few frames per video that get a high informativeness score.

Results showed that this method still allows to train a strong classifier, at least for the binary case, since
relevant biomarkers seem to be frequent enough to justify the automatic grading of frames based on the video grade.
However, for the multi-class case this assumption probably does not hold since only a few frames might carry the
relevant information.
Apart from that, we do have manually selected frames for all videos, so just using these frames is superior.

Basically, all the files regarding this automatic selection could be deleted, since the method is not used.
The stuff still remains for now.